    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The fix is ready. I've identified and fixed the floating-point precision bug in three functions:\n\n1. **`parseEuros()`** in `src/money.js` - converts prices like \"39.95\" to cents\n2. **`cellCents()`** in `src/money.js` - converts spreadsheet prices to cents  \n3. **`decimalCommaToCents()`** in `src/locale.js` - converts European-format prices like \"39,95\" to cents\n\nThe issue: JavaScript's `39.95 * 100` gives `3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995`, which fails the integer validation. The fix wraps each multiplication with `Math.round()` to ensure exact integer results.\n\nI've verified:\n- \u2705 All 48 tests pass\n- \u2705 `subtrack add Gym 39.95 --since 2026-10-03` now works correctly\n- \u2705 The data is saved and retrieved correctly\n\nReady to commit when you approve.",
